From: yclu4 <yclu4@nuvoton.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] compositor/wayland-egl: define QT_EGL_NO_X11 for no-X11 targets

Mesa's eglplatform.h selects the EGL native type by probing preprocessor
macros in order:
  WL_EGL_PLATFORM -> Wayland types
  __GBM__         -> GBM types
  USE_OZONE       -> intptr_t stubs
  USE_X11         -> includes <X11/Xlib.h>
  __unix__        -> void* fallback (only if none of the above match)

When the compositor wayland-egl hardware-integration plugin is compiled,
none of the Wayland/GBM/Ozone guards appear in CXXFLAGS (egl.pc Cflags is
empty on Mesa), so the header falls through to USE_X11 and tries to include
<X11/Xlib.h>. On an embedded target without X11 headers this is a fatal
error.

Qt5Base already solves the same problem for its own EGL support code with
-DQT_EGL_NO_X11, which makes QtEglSupport use safe internal typedefs
instead of the raw eglplatform.h types. Add the same define to
wayland-egl.pri so the compositor plugin compiles cleanly without an X11
sysroot.

Signed-off-by: yclu4 <yclu4@nuvoton.com>
---
 src/hardwareintegration/compositor/wayland-egl/wayland-egl.pri | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hardwareintegration/compositor/wayland-egl/wayland-egl.pri b/src/hardwareintegration/compositor/wayland-egl/wayland-egl.pri
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/src/hardwareintegration/compositor/wayland-egl/wayland-egl.pri
+++ b/src/hardwareintegration/compositor/wayland-egl/wayland-egl.pri
@@ -4,6 +4,14 @@
 
 QT += egl_support-private
 
+# Mesa's eglplatform.h has no safe fallback for non-X11 embedded targets:
+# if none of WL_EGL_PLATFORM / __GBM__ / USE_OZONE / ANDROID is defined it
+# falls through to USE_X11 and includes <X11/Xlib.h>, which does not exist
+# in this sysroot.  Qt5Base already guards its own EGL support code with
+# QT_EGL_NO_X11; apply the same define here so the compositor wayland-egl
+# hardware-integration plugin compiles cleanly without an X11 sysroot.
+DEFINES += QT_EGL_NO_X11
+
 SOURCES += \
     $$PWD/waylandeglclientbufferintegration.cpp
 
